│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ waterfilling_vectorized_eplb                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the two programs (which differ only in `balanced_packing`): keep the         │
│                          │ vectorized layer-parallel `balanced_packing` from the current program (fastest algorithm  │
│                          │ time), and replace the sequential `replicate_experts` loop with a vectorized              │
│                          │ water-filling approach. The replica counts are computed with a binary search on the load  │
│                          │ threshold T: each expert gets c_i = max(1, ceil(w_i/T)), and we find the minimal T such   │
│                          │ that sum(c_i) <= num_phy. Remaining slots are then handed out greedily (few iterations,   │
│                          │ fully vectorized per step). Finally, `phy2log`/`rank` are constructed directly from the   │
│                          │ counts via `repeat_interleave` instead of a Python loop over every redundant expert. This │
│                          │ reduces the algorithm runtime (O(log) binary-search steps + few extras instead of         │
│                          │ O(num_redundant) tensor ops per step) while giving at least as good load balance          │
│                          │ (water-filling is the optimal greedy for minimizing max w_i/c_i), improving both the      │
│                          │ speed and expert-level balancedness. Inputs/outputs unchanged.                            │
