│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ greedy_lpt_vectorized_packing                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current snake (boustrophedon) packing is very fast but produces substantially worse   │
│                          │ pack balance than the classic greedy longest-processing-time (LPT) assignment, which is   │
│                          │ reflected in the low GPU/expert balancedness scores. The prior program used true greedy   │
│                          │ assignment but with a doubly-nested Python loop (one iteration per layer per group),      │
│                          │ making it too slow. Here we restore the greedy "assign the next heaviest item to the      │
│                          │ least-loaded pack that still has capacity" policy, but vectorize the layer dimension: we  │
│                          │ only loop over the sorted item positions (num_groups iterations), and each iteration uses │
│                          │ a handful of small tensor ops across all rows simultaneously. This recovers greedy-level  │
│                          │ balance (better balancedness scores) at a fraction of the original Python-loop cost,      │
│                          │ improving the combined score.                                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
