│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ vectorized_rounded_greedy_packing                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The main bottleneck is `balanced_packing`: it runs a Python double loop (num_layers ×     │
│                          │ num_items) with per-item `min(...)` scans and tensor iteration, which is extremely slow   │
│                          │ (speed_score 0.00). I replace it with a "round-based greedy" heuristic that is            │
│                          │ mathematically equivalent in spirit to LPT but fully vectorized across all layers:        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Sort each layer's items by descending weight once.                                      │
│                          │ - Process items in rounds of `num_packs` (each pack must receive exactly                  │
│                          │ `groups_per_pack` items, so there are exactly `groups_per_pack` rounds).                  │
│                          │ - In each round, take the `num_packs` heaviest remaining items (already sorted) and       │
│                          │ assign the heaviest to the currently lightest pack, second heaviest to second lightest,   │
│                          │ etc. Each round is a single argsort over pack weights plus a couple of scatter/gather     │
│                          │ ops, all executed for every layer at once on the tensor.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces the Python loop from O(num_layers × num_items) iterations (each doing an     │
│                          │ O(num_packs) Python `min`) to O(groups_per_pack) fully vectorized torch iterations,       │
│                          │ typically a 1-2 order of magnitude speedup, while preserving near-LPT balancedness        │
│                          │ (pairing heavy items with light packs each round).                                        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
