│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ global_lpt_swap_refined                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current hierarchical approach packs whole expert groups to fixed-size node buckets    │
│                          │ first, then replicates within each node with an equal number of physical slots per node.  │
│                          │ Since node token loads are unequal but slot counts are fixed, this creates systematic     │
│                          │ per-expert load imbalance (expert balancedness 0.25) and cross-node GPU imbalance.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new approach drops the node hierarchy entirely and solves the problem globally in two │
│                          │ stages:                                                                                   │
│                          │ 1. Global water-filling replication: replicas are assigned to the hottest logical experts │
│                          │ across the whole layer (vectorized over all layers simultaneously), which equalizes       │
│                          │ per-replica load `w_j/c_j` globally rather than per-node, directly improving expert       │
│                          │ balancedness.                                                                             │
│                          │ 2. Global LPT packing to GPUs with exact cardinality constraints (heap-based              │
│                          │ longest-processing-time-first), followed by a pairwise swap local-search refinement       │
│                          │ between the heaviest and lightest GPU that provably reduces the maximum GPU load until no │
│                          │ improving swap exists. This improves GPU balancedness beyond plain greedy.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It also runs fully on vectorized NumPy with only short Python loops (num_redundant        │
│                          │ iterations for replication, one heap pass + bounded refinement per layer for packing),    │
│                          │ keeping algorithm runtime very low.                                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
