│ patch_description        │ Gen 9's per-node replication (Step 2 operating on node-local expert subsets) caps         │
│                          │ achievable expert balance: each node can only replicate among its own experts, and a hot  │
│                          │ expert confined to one node cannot receive replicas from the global redundant pool. We    │
│                          │ restructure the hierarchy to replicate globally first: run `replicate_experts` on the     │
│                          │ full logical expert set with the full `num_physical_experts` pool, so the water-filling   │
│                          │ greedy allocates every redundant slot to whichever expert has the highest per-replica     │
│                          │ load across all layers, unconstrained by node membership. Then the physical replicas      │
│                          │ (with their halved/shared loads) are packed to GPUs with a single global                  │
│                          │ `balanced_packing` call. This swaps the order of Steps 1/2 as suggested, and should       │
│                          │ substantially raise `balancedness_score_expert` (the weakest metric at 0.25) while        │
│                          │ keeping GPU-level LPT packing quality, since the packing stage now sees globally balanced │
│                          │ replica weights.                                                                          │
