│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the three programs. Key insight: the current program is the fastest          │
│                          │ (times_algorithm 0.01) thanks to vectorized packing, but its per-step greedy loop is      │
│                          │ still O(num_groups) iterations. The inspiration program's serpentine (snake) packing is   │
│                          │ fully vectorized in a single scatter — fastest of all. Meanwhile, the current/second      │
│                          │ program's replicate_experts gain formula (weight/logcnt) produced the better expert       │
│                          │ balancedness score (0.25 vs 0.24) compared to the weight/(cnt*(cnt+1)) marginal-gain      │
│                          │ formula. So the crossover takes: (1) serpentine vectorized balanced_packing from the      │
│                          │ inspiration program for maximum speed, and (2) the weight/logcnt greedy replication from  │
│                          │ the current program for the better expert balancedness, keeping everything else           │
│                          │ (hierarchical pipeline, inverse permutation, log2phy scatter) identical to the shared     │
│                          │ skeleton. This should keep balancedness at ~0.25/0.66 while minimizing algorithm          │
│                          │ execution time.                                                                           │
