│ patch_description        │ Replace the per-item Python greedy loops with two fully vectorized heuristics: (1)        │
│                          │ replication counts computed in one shot via proportional water-filling (`c_i ≈ w_i *      │
│                          │ num_phy / total`, corrected by rounding to hit the exact total with min 1) instead of     │
│                          │ `num_redundant` sequential argmax iterations — this both lowers max replica load and      │
│                          │ drops an O(R) loop; (2) packing via "sorted snake packing": sort weights descending,      │
│                          │ split into consecutive blocks of `num_packs`, and assign blocks alternately in reverse    │
│                          │ order (snake) — a classic cardinality-constrained LPT-style heuristic with near-optimal   │
│                          │ max-load, done entirely in tensor ops (no per-item loop), drastically cutting algorithm   │
│                          │ execution time while retaining the hierarchical group→node→GPU structure and the exact    │
│                          │ same inputs/outputs.                                                                      │
