│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ global_replication_then_gpu_packing                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Two changes:                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Revert the snake packing** in `balanced_packing` back to the greedy least-loaded     │
│                          │ assignment. The measured metrics show the vectorized snake assignment regressed both      │
│                          │ `times_algorithm` (0.55 → 0.00) and `times_inference` (0.97 → 0.26) while leaving         │
│                          │ balancedness unchanged — it is strictly worse than the original greedy version, so        │
│                          │ restore the greedy loop.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Replicate experts globally before packing**, per the recommendation. The per-node    │
│                          │ replication in old Step 2 caps achievable expert balance: each node only redistributes    │
│                          │ its own `num_log/num_nodes` experts over its own slot budget, so a hot expert cannot gain │
│                          │ replicas by borrowing capacity from other nodes (expert balancedness is only 0.25).       │
│                          │ Instead, run `replicate_experts` once on the full logical expert set with the full        │
│                          │ `num_physical_experts` budget (marginal-gain `weight/cnt` picks the globally hottest      │
│                          │ experts for replication), then pack the resulting physical replicas directly onto all     │
│                          │ GPUs with `balanced_packing`. This gives every hot expert access to the whole replica     │
│                          │ pool (Step 1's node grouping was only a communication heuristic; replica slots need not   │
│                          │ respect it), and the greedy packing then equalizes per-GPU load across the entire pool.   │
│                          │ The final `phy2log`/`phyrank`/`logcnt` shapes are unchanged, so the `rebalance_experts`   │
│                          │ entry point and its `log2phy` scatter still work verbatim.                                │
