│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ gpu_lpt_swap_refine                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Key changes vs the current hierarchical implementation:                                   │
│                          │ 1. **Global policy instead of hierarchical**: always replicate experts globally with      │
│                          │ water-filling (`weight/logcnt`) and pack physical slots onto GPUs with                    │
│                          │ cardinality-constrained LPT, dropping the group→node hierarchy that produced the lower    │
│                          │ GPU balancedness (0.66 vs 0.76 for the global variant).                                   │
│                          │ 2. **Heavy↔light GPU swap local search**: after greedy LPT packing, repeatedly find the   │
│                          │ heaviest and lightest GPU per layer and evaluate *all* per_gpu×per_gpu slot swaps in one  │
│                          │ batched tensor op, applying the swap that minimizes max(new_heavy, new_light). This       │
│                          │ directly targets the max-GPU-load metric (GPU balancedness + inference time), running     │
│                          │ fully vectorized across all layers.                                                       │
│                          │ 3. **No CPU round-trip**: the current code does `weight.float().cpu()`; all ops (sorting, │
│                          │ packing, refinement) are already batched tensor kernels, so we stay on the input device,  │
│                          │ removing the dominant device-transfer cost from both algorithm and inference timing.      │
│                          │ 4. **Parameters**: refinement runs up to 64 rounds with early stop when no layer improves │
│                          │ by >1e-12; LPT packing uses least-loaded-with-capacity greedy (same as before);           │
│                          │ replication uses water-filling argmax of `weight/logcnt`.                                 │
