                        Patch Metadata - Gen 22/100 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ gpu_ondevice_batched_replication                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This version combines the three best-performing changes from prior generations, all of    │
│                          │ which address the dominant inference-time cost:                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Remove the `.cpu()` round-trip** in `rebalance_experts` (as recommended): the weight │
│                          │ tensor stays on its original device with a single `.float()` cast. All downstream kernels │
│                          │ (sort, gather, scatter) run on-device, eliminating host copies and slow CPU kernel        │
│                          │ execution. This is what gave Gen 2 its best `times_inference` of 0.23.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Batched top-k replication** in `replicate_experts`: instead of a Python loop of      │
│                          │ `O(num_redundant)` iterations (each with a `.max()` reduction and scatter updates), we    │
│                          │ compute the static marginal-gain table `w/(j*(j+1))` for all candidate duplicate ranks    │
│                          │ `j` at once, and take a single sorted `topk`. Since gains strictly decrease in `j` for a  │
│                          │ given expert, the sorted top-k order exactly reproduces the sequential greedy pick order, │
│                          │ so the mapping quality is identical while the loop collapses to one vectorized op.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Vectorized greedy LPT balanced_packing** (from the current best lineage): the        │
│                          │ per-item loop runs once per item position across all layers simultaneously via            │
│                          │ `argmin`/`scatter_`, giving the good GPU balancedness (0.67) while keeping algorithm time │
│                          │ tiny. The `ones` tensor is hoisted out of the loop.                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Same inputs/outputs as the original entry point.                                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0236                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
