│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ global_lpt_swap_refine                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current best version already uses global replication (which lifted GPU balancedness   │
│                          │ to 0.76), but its Python-per-layer greedy packing loop is the main time cost, and its     │
│                          │ packing quality is capped by plain LPT. My design keeps global replication but replaces   │
│                          │ the hierarchical machinery with two novel components: (1) a fully batched LPT packer — a  │
│                          │ single Python loop over sorted item positions, but every operation is a vectorized tensor │
│                          │ op across all layers at once, using masked argmin to respect per-GPU slot capacity; (2) a │
│                          │ vectorized max/min-pack swap refinement pass that repeatedly moves the heaviest item from │
│                          │ the most-loaded GPU to the least-loaded GPU (guaranteed strict decrease of max GPU load), │
│                          │ which pushes balance beyond what one-shot greedy can achieve. Rank-in-pack is recomputed  │
│                          │ in one vectorized sort after refinement. This draws on the snake-packing program's        │
│                          │ insight (vectorization for speed) and the greedy program's insight (quality), combining   │
│                          │ them with a novel refinement loop that neither had.                                       │
