│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lpt_swap_refinement                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Improves on the vectorized greedy LPT packing by adding a fully-vectorized local-swap     │
│                          │ refinement pass: for each row, repeatedly identify the heaviest-loaded pack and           │
│                          │ lightest-loaded pack, then swap the largest item in the overloaded pack with the smallest │
│                          │ item in the underloaded pack whenever it reduces the load spread (a > b). This goes       │
│                          │ beyond LPT's 4/3-approximation while keeping O(k·num_packs) batched ops (constant number  │
│                          │ of kernel launches per iteration), so algorithm time stays ~0. Also uses the batched      │
│                          │ top-k marginal-gain replication (provably identical to sequential greedy) to cut the      │
│                          │ replication loop, and avoids the CPU round-trip of the weight tensor, matching the        │
│                          │ fastest prior variant. Both the group-to-node packing and the physical-expert-to-GPU      │
│                          │ packing benefit from the refinement, improving GPU balancedness without hurting speed.    │
