│ patch_description        │ Key changes vs the current program: (1) keep the fast global (non-hierarchical)           │
│                          │ replication + LPT packing pipeline that achieved the best GPU balancedness (0.76) and     │
│                          │ runtime; (2) replace the slow, ineffective single heavy↔lightest refinement loop with a   │
│                          │ vectorized top-K refinement: each round it evaluates the best swap between every (heavy   │
│                          │ GPU in top-K by load) × (all other GPUs) pair via a batched numpy computation, accepting  │
│                          │ the swap that minimizes the resulting max GPU load — directly attacking the GPU           │
│                          │ balancedness ceiling while staying O(rounds) in Python iterations; (3) use the correct    │
│                          │ marginal-gain greedy w/(c*(c+1)) for replication to improve expert-level balancedness;    │
│                          │ (4) cap refinement rounds (e.g. 3*num_phy) so runtime stays low.                          │
